---
// About page illustration: a big coffee mug at the center of its own little
// solar system, with four moons orbiting it: run, family, tech, and faith.
// Steam curls up from the mug, and the site's logo star is on the front.
//
// Same setup as the other illustrations:
// viewBox is 400 wide, 260 tall. (0,0) is top-left, y grows DOWN.
// The moons follow an invisible ellipse (no orbit is drawn):
// center (200,140), radii 160 x 66, tilted -10 degrees.
// Moons on the back half are drawn before the mug, so they slip behind it.
// Moon sizes, largest to smallest: faith, family, tech, run.
//
// Each moon exists twice: a "back" copy (drawn behind the mug) and a
// "front" copy (drawn on top). Only one is visible at a time, swapped at the
// orbit's two ends, so a moon looks like it travels all the way around.
// The shoe faces the way it travels: left on the front half, right on the back.
//
// Motion (all CSS, in the <style> block below):
//   - .badge        the four moons travel the orbit, spaced evenly
//   - .steam        steam curls rise and fade
//   - .float        starbursts drift up and down
//   - .twinkle      sparkles pulse (shared class from global.css)
// Everything stops for visitors with "reduce motion" turned on, and the
// moons park in fixed spots around the orbit instead.
//
// Note: moon icons are drawn around (0,0) with no transform attributes,
// because iOS Safari drops SVG transforms on elements that use offset-path.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 400 260" class="about-art" aria-hidden="true">

  <!-- 2. Moons, BACK copies (drawn before the mug so it covers them) -->
  <g class="badge back b-run">
    <circle r="14" fill="#A9BFA4"></circle>
    <circle cx="-7.5" cy="-7.5" r="2.1" fill="#7D9480"></circle><circle cx="8.4" cy="7.5" r="1.5" fill="#7D9480"></circle>
    <path d="M0,-14 A14,14 0 0 1 0,14 A9.8,14 0 0 0 0,-14 Z" fill="#2A2118" opacity="0.12"></path>
    <circle r="14" fill="none" stroke="#2A2118" stroke-width="2.5"></circle>
